<.shell current={:copy_button}>
  <h1>Copy button</h1>
  <p class="lead">Copies the value before it.</p>

  <div class="demo max-w-sm">
    <dl>
      <dt>Latitude and longitude</dt>
      <dd>
        <.copy_button
          text="49.64310,-123.20890"
          id="copy-button-demo"
          value="49.64310,-123.20890"
          label="Copy latitude and longitude"
        />
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <h3>In a code block</h3>
  <div class="demo max-w-md">
    <.copy_code_block
      id="copy-button-demo-block"
      value="claude mcp add --transport http sarduty https://sarduty.com/teams/sfsar/mcp"
      label="Copy command"
    />
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    After a value people paste somewhere else: an address, a latitude and longitude, an email, or a phone number. In the corner of a code block people paste, such as a token or a command.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>
    A link someone sends or prints, such as a team's Take attendance page. Use a
    <a href={page_path(:button)}>button</a>
    that says Copy link.
  </p>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.copy_button text=&#123;…&#125; id="…" value=&#123;…&#125; label="Copy address" /&gt;</code>
    shows the text, then the button. The text's last word and the button stay on one line, so the button never wraps alone. Add
    <code>href</code>
    to make the text a link, such as an email. It shows Copied beside it for 2 seconds. The label is for screen readers and the tooltip. On a touch screen its tap area is 44px.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.copy_code_block id="…" value=&#123;…&#125; label="Copy token" /&gt;</code>
    for a code block, with the button in its top-right corner.
  </p>
</.shell>
